{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpsRNxMv4fQWY7zaVDZu36","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd049-realpath\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/realpath: Print Resolved Absolute Paths\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Build systems and deployment scripts resolve symbolic links and relative path components\n6\t  to obtain canonical absolute paths. realpath handles symlink chains, . and .. components,\n7\t  and missing path segments depending on mode flags. The Go implementation must match the\n8\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (grealpath, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout\n9\t  and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the resolved absolute pathname for each argument, one per line.\n13\t  - G2: Support existence modes (-e, -m) and symlink resolution control (-s).\n14\t  - G3: Support relative path output via --relative-to and --relative-base.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Default behavior and existence modes\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: When invoked with one or more path arguments and no flags, must resolve each path to its canonical absolute form (all symlinks resolved, no . or .. components) and print one per line, exiting 0.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: If the resolved path does not exist by default, must print an error to stderr and exit 1 for that operand.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: \"-e (--canonicalize-existing) requires that every component of the path exists. If any component is missing, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\"\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"-m (--canonicalize-missing) requires no component to exist. Must resolve as far as possible and construct the remainder without checking existence.\"\n28\t      - R1.5:\n29\t          text: \"-s (--strip, --no-symlinks) must not resolve symlinks; only clean . and .. components and prepend the working directory for relative paths.\"\n30\t\n31\t  R2:\n32\t    title: Relative path output\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R2.1:\n35\t          text: \"--relative-to=DIR must print each resolved path relative to DIR instead of as an absolute path.\"\n36\t      - R2.2:\n37\t          text: \"--relative-base=DIR must print paths relative to DIR when the resolved path starts with DIR; otherwise print the absolute path.\"\n38\t      - R2.3:\n39\t          text: When both --relative-to and --relative-base are specified, --relative-to is applied only if the path starts with --relative-base.\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Error handling\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: If no operand is provided, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: When multiple paths are given and some fail, must print errors for the failing paths and exit 1 (but still print successful resolutions).\n50\t\n51\t  R4:\n52\t    title: Differential testing\n53\t    items:\n54\t      - R4.1:\n55\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (grealpath) via pkg/testutils.\n56\t      - R4.2:\n57\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default resolution, -e with existing and missing paths, -m with missing paths, -s without symlink resolution, --relative-to, --relative-base, multiple operands with mixed success, and error cases.\"\n58\t      - R4.3:\n59\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n60\t\n61\tnon_goals:\n62\t  - cmd/realpath does not create files or directories.\n63\t  - cmd/realpath does not modify symbolic links.\n64\t\n65\tacceptance_criteria:\n66\t  - id: AC1\n67\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath /tmp prints the canonical path, matching grealpath.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R1.3\n72\t      - R1.4\n73\t      - R1.5\n74\t  - id: AC2\n75\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath -e /nonexistent exits 1 with an error, matching grealpath.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R1.1\n78\t      - R1.2\n79\t      - R1.3\n80\t      - R3.1\n81\t      - R3.2\n82\t      - R3.3\n83\t      - R4.1\n84\t      - R4.2\n85\t  - id: AC3\n86\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath -m /nonexistent/foo prints the constructed path, matching grealpath.\"\n87\t    traces:\n88\t      - R1.4\n89\t      - R4.2\n90\t  - id: AC4\n91\t    criterion: \"Differential test against grealpath passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n92\t    traces:\n93\t      - R1.2\n94\t      - R1.3\n95\t      - R3.1\n96\t      - R3.2\n97\t      - R3.3\n98\t      - R4.1\n99\t      - R4.2\n100\t      - R4.3\n101\t  - id: AC5\n102\t    criterion: \"cmd/realpath compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n103\t    traces:\n104\t      - R1.1\n105\t      - R1.2\n106\t      - R1.3\n107\t      - R1.4\n108\t      - R1.5\n109\t      - R2.1\n110\t      - R2.2\n111\t      - R2.3\n112\t      - R3.1\n113\t      - R3.2\n114\t      - R3.3\n115\t      - R4.1\n116\t      - R4.2\n117\t      - R4.3\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"663efcfa-d5c2-4e69-8f3a-88c2e6a05463","uuid":"8d713452-7723-41b1-9f19-a8b407e3e983","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:18:16.667Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5243/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd049-realpath.yaml","content":"id: srd049-realpath\ntitle: \"cmd/realpath: Print Resolved Absolute Paths\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Build systems and deployment scripts resolve symbolic links and relative path components\n  to obtain canonical absolute paths. realpath handles symlink chains, . and .. components,\n  and missing path segments depending on mode flags. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (grealpath, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout\n  and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the resolved absolute pathname for each argument, one per line.\n  - G2: Support existence modes (-e, -m) and symlink resolution control (-s).\n  - G3: Support relative path output via --relative-to and --relative-base.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and existence modes\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with one or more path arguments and no flags, must resolve each path to its canonical absolute form (all symlinks resolved, no . or .. components) and print one per line, exiting 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: If the resolved path does not exist by default, must print an error to stderr and exit 1 for that operand.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-e (--canonicalize-existing) requires that every component of the path exists. If any component is missing, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-m (--canonicalize-missing) requires no component to exist. Must resolve as far as possible and construct the remainder without checking existence.\"\n      - R1.5:\n          text: \"-s (--strip, --no-symlinks) must not resolve symlinks; only clean . and .. components and prepend the working directory for relative paths.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Relative path output\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"--relative-to=DIR must print each resolved path relative to DIR instead of as an absolute path.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"--relative-base=DIR must print paths relative to DIR when the resolved path starts with DIR; otherwise print the absolute path.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: When both --relative-to and --relative-base are specified, --relative-to is applied only if the path starts with --relative-base.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: If no operand is provided, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: When multiple paths are given and some fail, must print errors for the failing paths and exit 1 (but still print successful resolutions).\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (grealpath) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default resolution, -e with existing and missing paths, -m with missing paths, -s without symlink resolution, --relative-to, --relative-base, multiple operands with mixed success, and error cases.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/realpath does not create files or directories.\n  - cmd/realpath does not modify symbolic links.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath /tmp prints the canonical path, matching grealpath.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath -e /nonexistent exits 1 with an error, matching grealpath.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/realpath -m /nonexistent/foo prints the constructed path, matching grealpath.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against grealpath passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/realpath compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
