{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5243: implement srd049-realpath requirements R3.1-R3.3 and R4.1 in the go-unix-utils project. This is a \"stitch\" task in an automated code generation pipeline. The task requires:\n   - R3.1: If no operand is provided, print usage error to stderr and exit 1\n   - R3.2: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1\n   - R3.3: When multiple paths given and some fail, print errors for failing paths and exit 1 (but still print successful resolutions)\n   - R4.1: Differential tests must compare stdout/exit codes between Go binary and grealpath reference binary\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/realpath/main.go` and `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go`. Design decisions require extending (not rewriting) existing code, using testutils.RunDiffTests with grealpath, adding new test cases to existing test slice, and setting LC_ALL=C.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` pattern: builds Go binary, finds reference binary via `exec.LookPath`, runs both with same inputs, compares stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - `pkg/testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize\n   - `NormalizeFunc` for normalizing binary name differences and stderr case differences in error messages\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Existing resolve modes: modeDefault, modeCanonE (--canonicalize-existing), modeCanonM (--canonicalize-missing)\n   - Flag parsing: supports short flags (-e, -m, -s), long flags (--strip, --no-symlinks, --relative-to, --relative-base), and -- separator\